{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "chatcmpl-tool-bed96e31b4649c40", "type": "tool_result", "content": "# AQAScore: Evaluating Semantic Alignment in Text-to-Audio Generation via Audio Question Answering\narXiv: 2601.14728\nAuthors: Chun-Yi Kuan, Kai-Wei Chang, Hung-yi Lee\nYear: 2026 | Venue: \nTopic: audio_understanding\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. We introduce AQAScore, an evaluation framework that reformulates text-to-audio alignment assessment as an audio question answering task.\n  2. We demonstrate through human-rated relevance, pairwise comparison, and compositional reasoning benchmarks that AQAScore achieves higher correlation with human judgments and greater sensitivity to semantic errors than similarity-based metrics.\n\nTags: Eval, Eval/LLM", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "17cabbeb-4110-4879-b2c6-8c2ab37431f0", "uuid": "0222ee3e-9b45-4626-a579-574b95ce91bf", "timestamp": "2026-08-06T06:15:33.608Z", "tool_use_result": {"stdout": "# AQAScore: Evaluating Semantic Alignment in Text-to-Audio Generation via Audio Question Answering\narXiv: 2601.14728\nAuthors: Chun-Yi Kuan, Kai-Wei Chang, Hung-yi Lee\nYear: 2026 | Venue: \nTopic: audio_understanding\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. We introduce AQAScore, an evaluation framework that reformulates text-to-audio alignment assessment as an audio question answering task.\n  2. We demonstrate through human-rated relevance, pairwise comparison, and compositional reasoning benchmarks that AQAScore achieves higher correlation with human judgments and greater sensitivity to semantic errors than similarity-based metrics.\n\nTags: Eval, Eval/LLM", "stderr": "", "interrupted": false, "isImage": false, "noOutputExpected": false}}
{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "chatcmpl-tool-9d3ce30582fc6797", "type": "tool_result", "content": "# SemanticVocoder: Bridging Audio Generation and Audio Understanding via Semantic Latents\narXiv: 2602.23333\nAuthors: Zeyu Xie, Chenxing Li, Qiao Jin, Xuenan Xu, Guanrou Yang, Wenfu Wang, Mengyue Wu, Dong Yu, Yuexian Zou\nYear: 2026 | Venue: \nTopic: vocoder\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. SemanticVocoder directly generates waveforms from semantic latents, eliminating reliance on VAE modules and their associated negative impacts.\n  2. The text-to-audio system powered by SemanticVocoder achieves state-of-the-art performance on AudioCaps with a Fréchet Distance of 12.823 and a Fréchet Audio Distance of 1.709.\n  3. SemanticVocoder bridges audio generation and understanding by enabling both tasks to be modeled within a shared semantic latent space.\n\nTags: Vocoder, Vocoder/Diffusion", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "17cabbeb-4110-4879-b2c6-8c2ab37431f0", "uuid": "c5bcf035-6aee-4761-a17f-1e067b8581e6", "timestamp": "2026-08-06T06:15:33.917Z", "tool_use_result": {"stdout": "# SemanticVocoder: Bridging Audio Generation and Audio Understanding via Semantic Latents\narXiv: 2602.23333\nAuthors: Zeyu Xie, Chenxing Li, Qiao Jin, Xuenan Xu, Guanrou Yang, Wenfu Wang, Mengyue Wu, Dong Yu, Yuexian Zou\nYear: 2026 | Venue: \nTopic: vocoder\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. SemanticVocoder directly generates waveforms from semantic latents, eliminating reliance on VAE modules and their associated negative impacts.\n  2. The text-to-audio system powered by SemanticVocoder achieves state-of-the-art performance on AudioCaps with a Fréchet Distance of 12.823 and a Fréchet Audio Distance of 1.709.\n  3. SemanticVocoder bridges audio generation and understanding by enabling both tasks to be modeled within a shared semantic latent space.\n\nTags: Vocoder, Vocoder/Diffusion", "stderr": "", "interrupted": false, "isImage": false, "noOutputExpected": false}}
{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "chatcmpl-tool-8d8c7487c91cbab2", "type": "tool_result", "content": "# \narXiv: 2605.00329\nAuthors: \nYear: 0 | Venue: \nTopic: tts_vc\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. The energy-distance objective is applied to text-to-audio generation for the first time, enabling low-latency one-step latent synthesis.\n  2. An auxiliary distillation loss aligns feature representations from a diffusion-based teacher transformer with the energy-based student model, yielding consistent improvements across all objective metrics.\n  3. The proposed model outperforms existing few-step sampling baselines on both objective and subjective metrics while narrowing the quality gap to multi-step diffusion systems.\n\nTags: TTS, TTS/架构-NAR-Diffusion, TTS/功能-蒸馏加速, TTS/功能-快速生成", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "17cabbeb-4110-4879-b2c6-8c2ab37431f0", "uuid": "78f31253-4cff-4db3-8f50-d53922a67770", "timestamp": "2026-08-06T06:15:34.249Z", "tool_use_result": {"stdout": "# \narXiv: 2605.00329\nAuthors: \nYear: 0 | Venue: \nTopic: tts_vc\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. The energy-distance objective is applied to text-to-audio generation for the first time, enabling low-latency one-step latent synthesis.\n  2. An auxiliary distillation loss aligns feature representations from a diffusion-based teacher transformer with the energy-based student model, yielding consistent improvements across all objective metrics.\n  3. The proposed model outperforms existing few-step sampling baselines on both objective and subjective metrics while narrowing the quality gap to multi-step diffusion systems.\n\nTags: TTS, TTS/架构-NAR-Diffusion, TTS/功能-蒸馏加速, TTS/功能-快速生成", "stderr": "", "interrupted": false, "isImage": false, "noOutputExpected": false}}
